%% Fastpack — sequence of a single `fpack build --development` run
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User (CLI)
    participant C as Commands.Build
    participant B as Builder
    participant G as DependencyGraph
    participant R as Resolver
    participant W as Worker pool (N=CPUs)
    participant N as node-service (webpack loaders)
    participant K as Cache/FSCache
    participant O as Bundle

    U->>C: fpack build --development
    C->>B: Config.term → Builder.make(config)
    B->>K: Cache.make(Load{...}) — load persistent cache if present
    B->>B: create tmp output dir .fpack-<rand>
    C->>B: Builder.build()
    B->>G: DependencyGraph.build(ctx, Main(entries), graph)
    loop per module (async, memoized via Lazy promises)
        G->>K: Cache.getModule(location)? (skip worker if fresh)
        G->>W: Reader.read(location, source) [Marshal request]
        W->>W: Preprocessor.run (chain)
        opt webpack loaders configured
            W->>N: JSON {loaders, filename, source}
            N-->>W: {source, deps, warnings, files}
        end
        W->>W: builtin transpilers + analyze (patch to __fastpack_require__)
        W-->>G: {source, static/dynamic deps, scope, exports, module_type}
        G->>R: resolve each dependency request
        R->>K: FSCache stat/read/readdir (+case-sensitivity check)
        G->>G: recurse into unseen resolved locations
    end
    B->>B: ExportFinder.ensure_exports (import name validation)
    B->>O: Bundle.make(graph, entry) — chunk by dynamic imports
    B->>O: Bundle.emit — write runtime + eval-wrapped modules to tmp dir
    O->>O: rename tmp dir → outputDir (atomic swap)
    C->>K: Cache.save (Marshal to node_modules/.cache/fpack)
    C-->>U: "Done in Xs. Bundle: NKb. Modules: M."
